# Dockerfile-scoped ignore for backend-ts/Dockerfile (issue #109 PR1 + slim-image deploy fix).
#
# Named "<dockerfile>.dockerignore" beside the Dockerfile so BuildKit uses THIS file (instead of any
# root .dockerignore) ONLY when building `-f backend-ts/Dockerfile <repo-root>`. Scoping it here keeps
# it from affecting other repo-root-context builds — notably infra/docker-compose.yml, which builds the
# Java backend + Next frontend with `context: ..` and COPYs backend/ and frontend/ (a root .dockerignore
# excluding those dirs would break that local/systemd stack).
#
# Patterns are relative to the build context root (the repo root). This image only COPYs ./backend-ts
# and ./external/mieweb-cloud, so everything else is excluded to trim the context, and installed deps /
# local state are dropped (re-installed in the image).
#
# Do NOT exclude backend-ts/measures/official/ — the vendored official measure bundles are
# runtime-loaded by wiring/official-artifacts.ts (fqm-execution fidelity-diff path, and the executor
# router once measures flip to official).
#
# SIZE WATCH (keep in sync with backend-ts/.dockerignore): ~10MB per measure, currently cms122 +
# cms125 = ~21MB. All 8 priority measures would be ~80MB. The deploy job-poll window already had to be
# raised once when the image outgrew it (PR #283). Before vendoring the remaining six, enable
# `vendor:official --strip-elm-annotations` (measured 79% smaller: 9.8MB → 2.1MB of ELM), gated on
# PR-6's MADiE suite proving it outcome-neutral — ELM localIds drive fqm's clause coverage.
#
# Test-case decks are NOT here: they are fetched to .official-content/ and gitignored.
#
# Do NOT exclude external/mieweb-cloud — workspace members live there.

.git
**/node_modules
**/.data
**/.npm
**/.pnpm-store
**/.cache
# Never leak a real env file into the image — anywhere in the context, incl. the
# external/mieweb-cloud submodule (a scoped backend-ts/.env rule would miss it).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
backend
frontend
e2e
docs
infra
scripts
*.pdf
*.md

# Host-side test / coverage noise under backend-ts (image re-installs deps; tests are not runtime)
backend-ts/coverage
backend-ts/**/*.log
backend-ts/.env
backend-ts/.env.*
backend-ts/**/*.tsbuildinfo
backend-ts/dist
backend-ts/build
